---
title: Use Case Diagram - ShiftChex
---
%% Mermaid has no UML use case diagram type. This is the usual workaround:
%% stadium shapes for use cases, a subgraph for the system boundary,
%% and dashed arrows for the include relationships. Both actors sit on the
%% left so the three include arrows can all flow the same direction.
flowchart LR
    Employee["Employee<br/>(actor)"]:::actor
    Manager["Manager<br/>(actor)"]:::actor

    subgraph ShiftChex
        UC01(["UC-01 Declare Weekly Availability"])
        UC02(["UC-02 Request Time Off"])
        UC03(["UC-03 View My Schedule"])
        UC04(["UC-04 Post Shift for Swap"])
        UC05(["UC-05 Claim Posted Shift"])
        UC06(["UC-06 Build Draft Schedule"])
        UC08(["UC-08 Publish Schedule"])
        UC09(["UC-09 Approve or Deny Swap"])
        UC10(["UC-10 Approve or Deny Time Off"])
        UC11(["UC-11 View Coverage and Labor Report"])
        UC07(["UC-07 Validate Schedule Against Rules"])
    end

    Employee --- UC01 & UC02 & UC03 & UC04 & UC05
    Manager --- UC06 & UC08 & UC09 & UC10 & UC11

    UC05 -. «include» .-> UC07
    UC06 -. «include» .-> UC07
    UC08 -. «include» .-> UC07

    classDef actor fill:#ffffff,stroke:#333333,stroke-width:2px,font-weight:bold
